'''Borut Javornik''' (born 14 April 1967 in [[Krka (Sava)|Krka]]) is a [[Yugoslavia|Yugoslav]]-born, [[Slovenia]]n [[whitewater slalom|slalom canoeist]] who competed from the mid-1980s to the mid-1990s. He won a bronze medal in the C-1 team event at the [[1989 ICF Canoe Slalom World Championships]] in [[Savage River (Maryland)|Savage River]]. He also finished 16th in the [[Canoeing at the 1992 Summer Olympics – Men's slalom C-1|C-1 event]] at the [[1992 Summer Olympics]] in [[Barcelona]].

